
DAYTIME(1)          UNIX Programmer's Manual           DAYTIME(1)

NAME
     daytime - give the time to human-reasonable accuracy

SYNOPSIS
     daytime

DESCRIPTION
     _D_a_y_t_i_m_e prints out in the English the current time of day,
     accurate to the nearest fifteen minutes.  Many people find
     this type of abstraction useful, since it doesn't really
     matter to them that it's 16:19 when all they wanted to know
     is that it's "Quarter past four."

BUGS
     _D_a_y_t_i_m_e depends on the user to determine whether it's
     currently night or day.

